{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists taking care of you. You're in the ICU because your blood sugar was very high and you're in diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA. Do you understand what that means?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been through this before. I think I forgot my insulin last night because I was drinking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely part of it. You had a pint of alcohol yesterday and missed your glargine. Your glucose was 751, and your pH was low at 7.04, which confirms DKA. We’ve started an insulin drip and are giving you IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been tired and just not checking my sugars. I know I should, but it’s hard with everything going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We also noticed your potassium was high at 5.7, but that’s improving with treatment. Your kidney function is affected too—your creatinine is up to 1.5, but we think it’s from dehydration, not new kidney disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? My mom has kidney problems from diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right now, it’s acute and likely reversible. Your baseline creatinine is 0.6, and with fluids, it’s already coming down. We’ve held your lisinopril for now to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my insulin? I was on 17 units glargine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping you on the insulin drip until your acid levels stabilize. Then we’ll restart glargine, probably at a lower dose—maybe 15 units. The endocrine team will help adjust your sliding scale too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had trouble sticking to my regimen. I’ve been depressed and drinking more since my cousin passed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. We’ve consulted Psychiatry. They want you in an outpatient program, but you refused inpatient. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I don’t want to be locked up. But I do want help. I keep messing up my health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re setting you up with a partial program—SOAP at ___—and a community support group through Vinfen. You’ll start intake in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds okay. I need to get better. My kids need me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing the right thing by being open. We also checked for infection—your chest X-ray was clear, flu test negative, and blood cultures show no growth. So no pneumonia or sepsis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count was high at 13.3, but that’s common in DKA and not always from infection. It’s already coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this dry cough. Is that from the DKA too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. It could also be from allergies—your history mentions rhinitis. But the X-ray shows no infection, so we’re not worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been itchy down there. Vaginal itching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-01-23 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of infection in your urine, and no discharge reported. It might be related to high sugar levels. Once your glucose is controlled, that should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are improving. Glucose is down to 176, bicarb up to 17, and anion gap is closing. We’re turning off the insulin drip soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I eat something? I’m really hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on a regular diet. You’ll need to check your blood sugar regularly and give your own insulin. We’ll help you with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been skipping my iron pills too. My last one was weeks ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ferritin is low at 12, confirming iron deficiency. You’re still menstruating, which likely contributes. We’ve restarted your ferrous sulfate. You’ll need to take it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. It upsets my stomach sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-01-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it with food or switch to a lower dose if needed. We’ll check your levels as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is now 1.0 and glucose is stable. You’re moving to the regular floor today. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Less tired. I’ve been checking my sugars like I should."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. The Psychiatry team met with you yesterday. Are you planning to go to the SOAP program?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m going next week. I think I need the support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re also sending you home with ketone test strips. Use them if your sugar is high, especially if you feel sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember using those before. I just forget when I’m not feeling well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-01-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The goal is to catch DKA early. We’ll go over your discharge meds tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning are looking good. Glucose 162, bicarb 20, creatinine 0.6—back to baseline. WBC is low at 2.5, but no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the low white count a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. It can happen after DKA. We’ll monitor it, but you’re not showing signs of illness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad my kidneys are okay. I worry about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So do we. Staying hydrated and managing your sugars is key. Your neuropathy and retinopathy also need regular follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been to my eye doctor in a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-01-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please schedule that. Same with your PCP. You need to keep all your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning discharge tomorrow if all stays stable. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be on the same insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 15 units of glargine at bedtime and use lispro on a sliding scale for highs. We adjusted it to reduce DKA risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—mirtazapine, Effexor, aspirin, statin, and your nasal spray. We’re continuing iron, thiamine, and folate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try to stay on them this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2161-01-27 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe in you. The support program will help. And call your doctor if your sugars are high or you feel unwell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2161-01-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last day in the hospital. Your exam is normal—clear lungs, normal heart, no swelling. You’re ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2161-01-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous. I don’t want to end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2161-01-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re setting you up for success. Keep your appointments, take your meds, and reach out for help when you need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2161-01-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2161-01-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. You’re strong for facing this. Let’s get your discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2161-01-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before discharge. You’ve done great. Any last concerns?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2161-01-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. I’ve got my prescriptions and follow-up dates."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2161-01-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember: ketone strips if sugar is high, call your doctor if vomiting or sick, and go to the ER if you can’t keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2161-01-29 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll take care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2161-01-29 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re proud of you. You’ve turned a corner. Take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2161-01-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge. You’ll go home today. Your condition is stable—alert, eating well, and walking independently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2161-01-30 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. I’ll start the program and see my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2161-01-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the plan. We’ll send all your records to your PCP. Call us if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2161-01-30 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I mean it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2161-01-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and stay healthy."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-01-23 14:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-01-30 16:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with type 1 diabetes, depression, and alcohol use disorder, was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) after missing insulin due to alcohol use and poor self-care. She presented with vomiting, polyuria, and polydipsia, with a glucose of 751, pH of 7.04, and anion gap of 37. She was treated with an insulin drip and IV fluids, with resolution of DKA and improvement in acute kidney injury, which was attributed to dehydration. Her insulin regimen was adjusted to 15 units of glargine at bedtime with a sliding scale. Psychiatric evaluation led to enrollment in an outpatient alcohol treatment program due to refusal of inpatient admission. Iron deficiency anemia was addressed with continued supplementation. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up plans for primary care, mental health, and diabetes management.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Severe nonproliferative diabetic retinopathy",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Alcohol abuse, unspecified",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Dehydration",
      "Allergic rhinitis, cause unspecified",
      "Other chronic allergic conjunctivitis"
    ]
  }
}
